    {
      "dom_id": "question-89407",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "It is known that $40%$ of a given population have blood type O$+.$ What is the variance of the number of people in a random sample of $100$ people having blood type O$+?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of people having blood type O$+.$\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=100$ people\n\n- the probability of finding a person with blood type O$+$ is $p=40%=0.4$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(100,0.4).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of people with blood type O$+$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(100)(0.4)(1-0.4) \\\\  & =(40)(0.6) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
